    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-calculus-2009-p5.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The derivative of a function is defined as \\(f^{\\prime}(x)=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\\). Iterating this formula four times yields\n\n\\[f^{(4)}(x)=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(x+4 h)-4 f(x+3 h)+6 f(x+2 h)-4 f(x+h)+f(x)}{h^{4}} .\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(f=\\sin\\) and \\(x=\\pi / 3\\), the expression is equal to \\(\\sin ^{(4)}(\\pi / 3)=\\sin (\\pi / 3)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\).",
      "hints": [],
